# Postgres connection string.
#
# Local development (Postgres running on this machine):
#   DATABASE_URL="postgresql://qbank:qbank@127.0.0.1:5432/aviation_qbank"
#
# Neon or Supabase: copy the connection string from the dashboard. It will
# already include ?sslmode=require, which is what you want.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/aviation_qbank"

# Optional. Number of Postgres connections this process may open. Default 5.
# Lower it to 1 on serverless platforms with a small connection allowance.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=5

# ── Password reset email ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Optional, and the app works without it: with no provider configured, the
# reset link is printed in the server log instead of sent. That is fine for
# local development — you read the link out of the terminal — and not fine
# for the deployed site, where nobody can see the log.
#
# To send real email, set both of these. RESEND_API_KEY comes from
# resend.com; EMAIL_FROM must be an address at a domain verified there.
# RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
# EMAIL_FROM="PilotQBank <noreply@your-domain.com>"

# Where links in those emails point. Set this on any deployment whose public
# address is not what Vercel reports — a custom domain, most obviously.
# Without it: Vercel's production domain, or http://localhost:3000 locally.
# APP_URL="https://aviation-qbank.vercel.app"

# ── Stripe (subscriptions) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Optional, and the app works without it: with no secret key configured,
# /upgrade says plainly that payments are not set up yet, and every student
# gets the free allowance and nothing more. Practising and every other
# feature work exactly as before.
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET come from the Stripe dashboard
# (Developers → API keys, and Developers → Webhooks for the endpoint's own
# signing secret once it exists) — never expose either anywhere a browser
# can read it.
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY should be a *restricted* key ("rk_live_…", created under
# Developers → API keys → Create restricted key) rather than the full secret
# key. This app asks Stripe for exactly one thing — a Checkout Session — so
# the only permission it needs is "Checkout Sessions: write"; everything else
# can be None. A full key in a hosting dashboard could refund charges and
# read every customer, to buy nothing. A live deployment handling real money
# is the case this matters most in.
#
# STRIPE_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID and STRIPE_QUARTERLY_PRICE_ID are the
# ids of two recurring Prices you create there — monthly, and every three
# months — each already carrying its own amount and interval; a price change
# is an edit in that dashboard, not here.
#
# The dashboard also needs a webhook endpoint pointed at this deployment's
# /api/webhooks/stripe, subscribed at least to customer.subscription.created,
# .updated and .deleted.
#
# Setting these in a hosting dashboard rather than a file: paste only the
# value into the value box — "sk_test_…", not "STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_…".
# `readEnv` strips that prefix, surrounding quotes and stray whitespace if
# they do get in, so a correct value transported badly still works, but the
# tidy thing is still to paste the value alone.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY="rk_..."
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET="whsec_..."
# STRIPE_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID="price_..."
# STRIPE_QUARTERLY_PRICE_ID="price_..."

# ── Owner tools ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Optional. The email address of the account that may generate gift codes
# at /owner/gift-codes (see the note on `provider` in the conventions),
# without a terminal or a database connection — anyone else visiting that
# path gets a plain 404, the same as if it did not exist. Must match the
# email an account signed up with exactly (case-insensitive).
# OWNER_EMAIL="you@example.com"

# ── Logbook Scanner ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Optional. With ANTHROPIC_API_KEY unset, /tools/logbook explains itself
# but scanning is off. The key is read only on the server
# (src/app/api/logbook/extract/route.ts) and never reaches a browser.
#
# LOGBOOK_MODEL defaults to claude-sonnet-5-5. If you change it, add its
# price to src/lib/logbook/pricing.ts or the owner's cost log reads "—".
# LOGBOOK_EFFORT is low | medium | high (default medium).
#
# LOGBOOK_PURCHASES_ENABLED is the feature flag for paying for an unlock.
# No payment provider is connected yet: leave it unset, and unlocks come
# from license codes (/owner/gift-codes, "One Logbook Scanner unlock"),
# manual grants (/owner/logbook) or a subscription's included one.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."
# LOGBOOK_MODEL="claude-sonnet-5-5"
# LOGBOOK_EFFORT="medium"
# LOGBOOK_PURCHASES_ENABLED="false"
